{
  "requirement": "When given `--path <crate-dir>` and no existing Habeas dev dependency, `habeas setup` MUST add that local crate as the dev dependency. Repeating setup MUST NOT add a duplicate Habeas dependency.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: the implementation looks right, but the test is too weak to count as covering the requirement.**\n\n**Implementation (looks correct)**\n- `src/main.rs` declares `Setup { path: Option<PathBuf> }` and dispatches it as `setup::run(path.as_deref())`.\n- In `src/setup.rs`, `run` (around lines 161–183, marked `{impl}` for this requirement) parses `Cargo.toml` and calls `has_habeas_dev_dependency`. That function, also marked `{impl}`, checks for a `habeas` key under `[dev-dependencies]`.\n- If no such dev dependency exists, `run` shells out to `cargo add --dev habeas --manifest-path <Cargo.toml>`. When `--path` is given it appends `--path <canonicalized crate-dir>`.\n- If the dependency already exists, `run` skips `cargo add`. A repeated setup therefore adds no second entry.\n- I found no unmarked behaviour that this requirement does not specify.\n\n**Tests (the weak point)**\n- The only `{test}` reference is `setup_is_repeatable` in `tests/setup.rs`. It runs `habeas setup --path <CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR>` twice on a fixture.\n- It then asserts only that `Cargo.toml` contains `[dev-dependencies]`, the substring `habeas`, and the substring `path = `.\n- It does not assert that the recorded path is the supplied crate directory. The substring `path = ` would match any path.\n- It does not assert that there is exactly one `habeas` entry. A duplicate would probably make the second run's manifest parse fail, but that is an indirect check.\n- It does not cover a manifest that already has a Habeas dev dependency, where the existing entry should be left untouched and `--path` ignored.\n- It does not cover a dependency declared only in `[dependencies]` or under a target table, or the failure path of `cargo add`.\n\n**Why this is false rather than true**\nThe central obligations are \"add *that local crate*\" and \"MUST NOT add a duplicate\". Neither is asserted precisely. The tests do not cover the interesting points in the design space (path value, no-duplicate count, pre-existing dependency preserved). The source contains no FIXME or other acknowledged gap, so I did not choose `FIXME`.",
  "inputs": [
